        "original_id": "dc3c15f2-9dac-5e60-bd4d-ef3158afb8d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1932 Maccabiah Games, Bar Kokhba revolt\n- Topics: commemorations, names of the revolt, Jewish revolts against Rome\n\nFacts:\n- The 1932 Maccabiah Games were held in commemoration of the 1800th anniversary of the Bar Kokhba revolt.\n- The Bar Kokhba revolt was a major rebellion by the Jews of Judaea Province against the Roman Empire.\n- Some historians refer to the Bar Kokhba revolt as the Second Revolt of Judea because they do not count the Kitos War of 115–117 CE, which was fought only marginally in Judea.",
